---
import Layout from '../../../components/Layout.astro';
import { official } from '../../../lib/orientdig.mjs';

const description = 'Understand what OrientDig does as a shopping agent, who supplies the item, and when you review photos and pay for freight.';
---
<Layout title="How the OrientDig Shopping Agent Works" description={description}>
  <article class="wrap page">
    <p><a class="text-link" href="/guides/how-to-buy/">How to use</a></p>
    <h1>How the OrientDig agent works</h1>
    <p class="lead">{description}</p>
    <div class="prose">
      <section class="content-block">
        <h2>The seller supplies the item</h2>
        <p>A Weidian listing provides the seller’s product photos, options, and size information. Start with the original listing and note the exact variant. Use the spreadsheet to compare listings and keep the item ID handy for later checks.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/categories/">Browse categories</a>
      </section>
      <section class="content-block">
        <h2>OrientDig handles the order and warehouse intake</h2>
        <p>Submit the listing and your variant through OrientDig. Check the item price and domestic delivery charge at checkout. Once it reaches the warehouse, open your own order to review the photos and check the current return or exchange terms if something looks wrong.</p>
        <a class="text-link" href="/guides/how-to-buy/">Follow the buying walkthrough</a>
      </section>
      <section class="content-block">
        <h2>You choose what to ship</h2>
        <p>After inspection, select the items for your international parcel. Compare the available routes using packed dimensions, weight, and destination. Review the final parcel quote and line restrictions before submitting it in your OrientDig account.</p>
        <div class="row"><a class="text-link" href="/guides/shipping/">Read the shipping guide</a><a class="text-link" href={official.help}>OrientDig help center</a></div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
